## What We Are Building

SandyStudio = AI animation studio (Next.js + Supabase + Inngest, local-first; `webapp/`). Today was 100% about closing the gap between «what Director sees in the animatic preview» and «what EXEC-STITCH actually ships as final cut». Director's overarching frustration entering today: timeline button 12 showed SH13 contents, his music fade/trim weren't audible in preview, sub-0.5s shots were still consuming time in the final cut, and his standing orders (1080p mandatory) kept getting lost between agent runs. Every commit today closes one of those leaks.

Pipeline status: 22/30 shots of E02 rendered. SH12 was the trigger that exposed the rest — its `IMG-anchor_start` had been stuck in REVIEW since 2026-06-03, so the animatic builder silently dropped it (Phase 1 audit), which then propagated as a `btn12 → SH13` misalignment everywhere. We fixed SH12 (anchor approved + plan content patched + VID v01 REVIEW rendered ≈ $2), regen-ed animatic to v07 with all 30 shots, then built systemic fixes so the same class of bug self-surfaces in the future.

