## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **SH12 first render attempt (without `planAssetId`)** — failed because runner.ts:1899 only loads the plan when `planAssetId` is in event data; without it `planStartAnchorAssetId` stays null and provider validation throws. Always pass explicit `planAssetId` when firing `sandystudio/exec-vgen/single-shot` directly.
- **SH12 second attempt (with patched plan but `quality_tier: fast`)** — failed with `422 — Input should be '480p' or '720p', input='1080p'`. Root: `seedance-with-end-image` alias forces standard tier in `resolveVanimProviderId`, but the body's `quality_tier: fast` later overwrote it; fast-tier model `bytedance/seedance-2.0/fast/image-to-video` caps at 720p. Animator's plan was internally inconsistent — fixed by patching `quality_tier: fast → standard` + cost note.
- **«30 кнопок но 29 в animatic»** — initial wrong guess. Director clarified «I see 29», not 30. Forced re-investigation that revealed SH12 was missing from `animatic_v1.shot_list` because its IMG-anchor START was stuck in REVIEW (status filter in `buildShotListFromAnchorChain`).
- **«Failed to load asset metadata» on every drawer click** — could not reproduce on server (all `/api/assets/{id}` returned 200; all 30 asset IDs from animatic v07 verified to exist in DB). Hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R) cleared it — was SWR cache poisoning from a prior session, no code fix needed.
- **Polина's batch regen of SH23 / SH25 / SH27 / SH29 plans (parallel work, no Director money-go)** — SH25 + SH29 came back 1080p OK; SH23 came back 480p, SH27 came back 720p. Director caught SH27 first; we found SH23 has same issue. Root: revision_note didn't reiterate «1080p mandatory»; Critic V13 only validates `resolution ∈ provider.supports_resolutions`, not a Director floor. The Bible-as-Standing-Orders plumbing landed today (commit `92f05df`) — Critic now sees Bible canon, so once Director writes the 1080p directive into `SS-S15-BIB-general_idea` and LOCKs it, the next regen pass should catch the violation.
- **Web Audio API for music preview shaping (Path A)** — rejected at plan stage in favour of server pre-process. Reason: Path A would have required a custom scrubber, AudioBufferSourceNode decode in RAM, and a new inline-video sync path; ~300 LoC for marginally faster preview update. Path B (ffmpeg on save) reuses existing `buildMusicAudioFilter` and is one new helper module + route extension.

